<section class="cs__sec" aria-labelledby="s1">
  <p class="st-k rv">01 · Challenge</p>
  <h2 class="cs__h rv" id="s1">A complex process, a promise of simplicity</h2>
  <p class="cs__p rv">
    International Visa and Travel Services (Pty) Ltd. (IVISATS) is a Johannesburg-based consultancy
    that helps individuals, families and businesses apply for visas. The client asked for a website
    that focuses on visa services, looks professional and trustworthy, and lives up to their slogan:
    “Making Visa Applications Simple”.
  </p>
  <div class="st-grid st-g4 st-wide">
    <div class="pcard rv">
      <p class="pcard__word">Question 01</p>
      <h3 class="pcard__title">Services</h3>
      <p class="pcard__text">Can IVISATS help with the visa I need, for where I’m going?</p>
    </div>
    <div class="pcard rv">
      <p class="pcard__word">Question 02</p>
      <h3 class="pcard__title">Trust</h3>
      <p class="pcard__text">Who are they, and can I rely on them with my application?</p>
    </div>
    <div class="pcard rv">
      <p class="pcard__word">Question 03</p>
      <h3 class="pcard__title">Process</h3>
      <p class="pcard__text">What will they do for me, and what happens next?</p>
    </div>
    <div class="pcard rv">
      <p class="pcard__word">Question 04</p>
      <h3 class="pcard__title">Contact</h3>
      <p class="pcard__text">How do I reach them about my destination and visa type?</p>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="st-callout rv">
    <p class="st-bh">
      How might we make a visa consultancy feel trustworthy at first glance, and turn an overwhelming
      process into one clear next step?
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="cs__sec" aria-labelledby="s2">
  <p class="st-k rv">02 · Defining the experience</p>
  <h2 class="cs__h rv" id="s2">Four pages, visas first</h2>
  <p class="cs__p rv">
    The company name includes Travel Services, but the client was clear that visas are the focus for
    now. The site has four core pages, each with one job, and leaves room for travel services and
    packages later.
  </p>
  <div class="st-stats st-wide rv">
    <div>
      <p class="st-stat">4</p>
      <p>core pages, each with one job</p>
    </div>
    <div>
      <p class="st-stat">6</p>
      <p>visa categories, each ending in Enquire Now</p>
    </div>
    <div>
      <p class="st-stat">5</p>
      <p>steps in How We Assist, from consultation to follow-up</p>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="st-grid st-g4 st-wide">
    <div class="pcard rv">
      <p class="pcard__word">Page 01</p>
      <h3 class="pcard__title">Home</h3>
      <p class="pcard__text">Introduce IVISATS and its slogan, and point visitors to the right service.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="pcard rv">
      <p class="pcard__word">Page 02</p>
      <h3 class="pcard__title">About Us</h3>
      <p class="pcard__text">Explain who the company is, its experience, mission and approach to clients.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="pcard rv">
      <p class="pcard__word">Page 03</p>
      <h3 class="pcard__title">Visa Services</h3>
      <p class="pcard__text">The main page: every visa category, the destinations, and how to enquire.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="pcard rv">
      <p class="pcard__word">Page 04</p>
      <h3 class="pcard__title">Contact Us</h3>
      <p class="pcard__text">Every contact channel, plus a visa enquiry form.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="cs__sec" aria-labelledby="s3">
  <p class="st-k rv">03 · Key UX decisions</p>
  <h2 class="cs__h rv" id="s3">Five decisions that keep it simple</h2>
  <p class="cs__p rv">
    Each decision answers one of the questions applicants arrive with. Follow a typical visit first,
    then see each decision beside the screen it shaped.
  </p>

  <h3 class="st-sub rv">Visitor journey: from first question to consultation</h3>
  <div class="st-wide st-tabset--steady rv">
    <div class="st-tabs" role="tablist" aria-label="Visitor journey steps">
      <button class="st-tab" type="button" role="tab" id="t-j1" aria-controls="p-j1">1. Land on the homepage</button>
      <button class="st-tab" type="button" role="tab" id="t-j2" aria-controls="p-j2">2. Find the visa</button>
      <button class="st-tab" type="button" role="tab" id="t-j3" aria-controls="p-j3">3. See how IVISATS helps</button>
      <button class="st-tab" type="button" role="tab" id="t-j4" aria-controls="p-j4">4. Enquire</button>
      <button class="st-tab" type="button" role="tab" id="t-j5" aria-controls="p-j5">5. Talk to a consultant</button>
    </div>
    <div class="st-gal" role="tabpanel" id="p-j1" aria-labelledby="t-j1">
      <p class="cs__p">“Making Visa Applications Simple” leads the page, with Book a Consultation and View Visa Services right below it.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="st-gal" role="tabpanel" id="p-j2" aria-labelledby="t-j2">
      <p class="cs__p">Six visa cards on the homepage lead to the Visa Services page, where each category is explained in full.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="st-gal" role="tabpanel" id="p-j3" aria-labelledby="t-j3">
      <p class="cs__p">Why Choose IVISATS and the five steps of How We Assist show what support to expect, and in which order.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="st-gal" role="tabpanel" id="p-j4" aria-labelledby="t-j4">
      <p class="cs__p">Every category ends in Enquire Now, which opens the Visa Enquiry Form.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="st-gal" role="tabpanel" id="p-j5" aria-labelledby="t-j5">
      <p class="cs__p">The visitor picks a destination and visa type and sends the form, or chats on WhatsApp straight away.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="st-split st-wide">
    <div class="st-split__text rv">
      <div class="st-decision">
        <p class="st-k">Decision A</p>
        <h3 class="st-bh">Lead with visas, leave room for travel</h3>
        <p class="cs__p">
          Visa services come right after the introduction on the homepage: six categories, each with
          one line on what IVISATS prepares. The footer lists the same six. Travel services can join
          later as a section of their own without changing the focus of these pages.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <figure class="cs__fig rv">
      <img
        src="{{ '/assets/images/projects/ivisats-home-services.webp' | rel }}"
        width="1400"
        height="818"
        alt="Homepage section titled Visa assistance for every reason you travel, with an All visa services link and six cards: Tourist and Visitor, Business, Study, Work-Related, Family and Spousal, and Transit Visas, each with a gold icon and a short description."
        loading="lazy"
        decoding="async"
      />
      <figcaption>Homepage visa overview, one card per reason to travel</figcaption>
    </figure>
  </div>

  <div class="st-split st-wide">
    <div class="st-split__text rv">
      <div class="st-decision">
        <p class="st-k">Decision B</p>
        <h3 class="st-bh">Show the process before asking for commitment</h3>
        <p class="cs__p">
          How We Assist lays out five steps, from consultation to follow-up, each with one sentence on
          what the client receives. The same process applies to every visa, so visitors always know
          which step comes next.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <figure class="cs__fig rv">
      <img
        src="{{ '/assets/images/projects/ivisats-home-steps.webp' | rel }}"
        width="1400"
        height="836"
        alt="How We Assist section titled Five steps, start to finish, with a Begin with step 1 button and five numbered steps: Consultation, Assessment of requirements, Document preparation and checking, Application assistance, and Follow-up."
        loading="lazy"
        decoding="async"
      />
      <figcaption>Five steps, the same for every visa</figcaption>
    </figure>
  </div>

  <div class="st-split st-wide">
    <div class="st-split__text rv">
      <div class="st-decision">
        <p class="st-k">Decision C</p>
        <h3 class="st-bh">End every service in an enquiry</h3>
        <p class="cs__p">
          On the Visa Services page, each category has its own row: who it is for, what IVISATS
          prepares, a practical tip, and an <strong>Enquire Now</strong> button. No service is a dead
          end.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <figure class="cs__fig rv">
      <img
        src="{{ '/assets/images/projects/ivisats-visa-categories.webp' | rel }}"
        width="1400"
        height="1274"
        alt="Visa categories we assist with: six rows for Tourist and Visitor, Business, Study, Work-Related, Family and Spousal, and Transit Visas, each with an icon, short tags, a description, a small practical note and an Enquire Now button on the right."
        loading="lazy"
        decoding="async"
      />
      <figcaption>Each visa category, with what’s covered and an Enquire Now button</figcaption>
    </figure>
  </div>

  <div class="st-split st-wide">
    <div class="st-split__text rv">
      <div class="st-decision">
        <p class="st-k">Decision D</p>
        <h3 class="st-bh">Ask for the details that matter</h3>
        <p class="cs__p">
          Besides name, email and phone, the enquiry form asks for applicant type, destination
          country, visa type, travel date and number of applicants. A consultant can reply with the
          requirements that apply, instead of a list of questions.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <figure class="cs__fig rv">
      <img
        src="{{ '/assets/images/projects/ivisats-form.webp' | rel }}"
        width="658"
        height="486"
        alt="Close-up of the Visa Enquiry Form: Applicant Type, Country You Want to Travel, and Type of Visa Required drop-downs, an Intended Travel Date field and a Number of Applicants field."
        loading="lazy"
        decoding="async"
      />
      <figcaption>Destination, visa type and travel date, asked up front</figcaption>
    </figure>
  </div>

  <div class="st-split st-wide">
    <div class="st-split__text rv">
      <div class="st-decision">
        <p class="st-k">Decision E</p>
        <h3 class="st-bh">Be honest about who decides</h3>
        <p class="cs__p">
          The FAQ answers “Can you guarantee my visa will be approved?” with “No consultancy can”,
          and an Important Notice says the final decision rests with the embassy, consulate or
          immigration authority. The About page repeats it: “We are a visa consultancy, not an
          immigration authority.” Setting expectations is part of being trustworthy.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <figure class="cs__fig rv">
      <img
        src="{{ '/assets/images/projects/ivisats-visa-faq.webp' | rel }}"
        width="1400"
        height="869"
        alt="Frequently asked questions in two columns, including Can you guarantee my visa will be approved, answered No consultancy can, followed by an Important Notice box explaining that requirements differ by country and the final decision rests with the embassy, consulate or immigration authority."
        loading="lazy"
        decoding="async"
      />
      <figcaption>FAQ and the Important Notice on the Visa Services page</figcaption>
    </figure>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="cs__sec" aria-labelledby="s4">
